---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'July 30, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — The HR Stack Guide"
  description="The terms governing your use of The HR Stack Guide, operated by Stack Guide Media."
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-14">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-slate-500">
          <li><a href="/" class="transition hover:text-indigo-600">Home</a></li>
          <li aria-hidden="true" class="text-slate-300">&gt;</li>
          <li class="font-medium text-indigo-600" aria-current="page">Terms of Service</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">
        Terms of Service
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-500">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </header>

    <article class="space-y-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
      <section>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of The HR Stack Guide (the "Site"),
          operated by Stack Guide Media ("Stack Guide Media," "we," "us," or "our"). By accessing or using the
          Site, you agree to be bound by these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the Site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Informational purpose only</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          Content on the Site, including vendor comparisons, ratings, pricing information, and feature
          matrices, is provided for general informational purposes only and does not constitute professional,
          legal, financial, or HR advice. Vendor pricing, features, and policies change over time; always
          confirm current details directly with the vendor before making a purchasing decision.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">No warranty</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          We aim to keep comparisons accurate and up to date, but the Site is provided on an "as is" and "as
          available" basis without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied, including but not
          limited to warranties of accuracy, completeness, or fitness for a particular purpose.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Affiliate relationships</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          The Site may contain affiliate links to third-party vendors. As described in our
          <a href="/affiliate-disclosure" class="font-medium text-indigo-600 hover:underline">Affiliate Disclosure</a>,
          we may earn a commission when you sign up for a vendor's product through these links, at no
          additional cost to you. Affiliate relationships do not influence our editorial ratings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Third-party websites</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          The Site links to third-party vendor websites that are not owned or controlled by Stack Guide Media.
          We are not responsible for the content, terms, or privacy practices of any third-party website. Your
          use of a third-party website is governed by that website's own terms and policies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, Stack Guide Media shall not be liable for any indirect,
          incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or any loss of profits or revenues, arising
          from your use of the Site or reliance on any information published on it, including decisions to
          purchase or subscribe to a vendor's product.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Intellectual property</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          Unless otherwise noted, the text, design, and original graphics on the Site are the property of Stack
          Guide Media and may not be reproduced or republished without prior written permission. Vendor names,
          logos, and trademarks referenced on the Site belong to their respective owners and are used for
          identification and comparison purposes only.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Changes to these Terms</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          We may update these Terms from time to time. Continued use of the Site after changes are posted
          constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms. The "Last updated" date above indicates when these
          Terms were last revised.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Contact us</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          Questions about these Terms can be sent to
          <a href="mailto:dave@thehrstackguide.com" class="font-medium text-indigo-600 hover:underline">dave@thehrstackguide.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
